{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789253668,"nonce":"GBnOGzN15ZUuC8bclLWMqAh8a5E=","title":"Python: the entry function inlines every library call it makes","message":"`__main__` and any function that calls the shared library many times\ninline the library bodies at each site; a short dict program produces\nthousands of SSA values in the entry function alone, and debug-build\ncompile time under the conformance harness runs into seconds. The\ninliner has no budget per caller, so the entry function, which is\ncalled once, pays the most for the least benefit.\n\nAn inlining budget per caller (or a policy that leaves functions\ncalled once alone) would cut compile time without touching hot code;\nlibrary functions marked as cold could stay out-of-line altogether.\nMeasure with the dict and set conformance programs under\nZYNTAX_DUMP_HIR_DIR before and after.","files":null}]}